{"key":"u3-008-v2","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"-1/5","working":"Differentiating both sides of 2x^2 - xy + y^2 = 8 with respect to x using implicit differentiation gives 4x - (y + x dy/dx) + 2y dy/dx = 0. Grouping dy/dx terms yields (2y - x) dy/dx = y - 4x, so dy/dx = (y - 4x) / (2y - x). Substituting the coordinates (x, y) = (1, 3), we get dy/dx = (3 - 4(1)) / (2(3) - 1) = -1/5.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":376,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":376,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":459,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":174,"reasoningTokens":285},"totalTokens":835,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":285,"promptTokenCount":376,"candidatesTokenCount":174,"totalTokenCount":835,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":376}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":174}]},"reasoningTokens":285,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4344,"keyed_label":"A"}
{"key":"u3-008-v2","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"audit","ok":true,"object":{"keyed_choice_correct":true,"per_choice":[{"label":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"label":"B","rationale_accurate":false,"issue":"Omitting only the term -x(dy/dx) from the derivative of -xy leaves 4x - y + 2y(dy/dx) = 0, which yields dy/dx = (y - 4x)/(2y) = -1/6 at (1, 3), not -4x/(2y) = -2/3 (which results from ignoring the -xy term entirely)."},{"label":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"label":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"other_defects":[]},"usage":{"inputTokens":650,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":650,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":1244,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":243,"reasoningTokens":1001},"totalTokens":1894,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":1001,"promptTokenCount":650,"candidatesTokenCount":243,"totalTokenCount":1894,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":650}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":243}]},"reasoningTokens":1001,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":9060,"keyed_label":"A"}
{"key":"u3-008-v2","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"-1/5","working":"Differentiate 2x^2 - xy + y^2 = 8 implicitly with respect to x:\n4x - (y + x dy/dx) + 2y dy/dx = 0.\nSo 4x - y - x dy/dx + 2y dy/dx = 0.\nCollect dy/dx terms:\n(-x + 2y) dy/dx + 4x - y = 0,\nso dy/dx = (y - 4x)/(2y - x).\nAt (1, 3): dy/dx = (3 - 4)/(6 - 1) = -1/5.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":430,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":174,"cacheReadTokens":256},"outputTokens":428,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":177,"reasoningTokens":251},"totalTokens":858,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":430,"completion_tokens":428,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":256,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":174,"total_tokens":858,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":256},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":251}},"reasoningTokens":251,"cachedInputTokens":256},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4921,"keyed_label":"A"}
